WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.841 --> 00:00:06.521
♪ intense electronic ♪

00:00:17.596 --> 00:00:18.596
[grunts]

00:00:33.787 --> 00:00:35.356
Morning, guys.

00:00:35.356 --> 00:00:37.908
Here in Karachi but not for long.

00:00:38.241 --> 00:00:39.921
Going out to the coast.

00:00:40.209 --> 00:00:42.163
Gadari, right? Gadari?

00:00:42.163 --> 00:00:44.263
-Gadani.
-Gadani. Gadani.

00:00:44.896 --> 00:00:49.228
One of the world's biggest
ship-breaking yards.

00:00:49.801 --> 00:00:54.762
Up to 1 million tons of metal
is scrapped per year from this place

00:00:54.762 --> 00:00:56.869
and it's not done through machines.

00:00:57.422 --> 00:01:02.089
It's done through human muscle,
sweat, and probably tears.

00:01:02.739 --> 00:01:07.861
So let's go on this adventure
and check out this very fascinating place.

00:01:11.480 --> 00:01:14.086
♪ intense electronic ♪

00:01:18.940 --> 00:01:20.640
[honking]

00:02:04.844 --> 00:02:06.150
Stuck in traffic.

00:02:06.150 --> 00:02:08.716
Crossed the line from Karachi
into Balochistan, right?

00:02:08.716 --> 00:02:09.716
-Yeah, right.

00:02:09.716 --> 00:02:11.114
-Balochistan right now.

00:02:11.114 --> 00:02:12.848
So a lot of security forces out.

00:02:12.848 --> 00:02:16.196
Lot of Rangers and policemen.

00:02:18.908 --> 00:02:20.268
[music continues]

00:02:39.837 --> 00:02:40.877
[door closes]

00:02:42.334 --> 00:02:43.454
Salam alaikum.

00:02:45.331 --> 00:02:46.331
Okay, guys.

00:02:47.315 --> 00:02:49.430
It's starting to get interesting.

00:02:49.430 --> 00:02:53.223
Saw a few boats from the car on the road.

00:02:53.223 --> 00:02:55.223
and then there's one out here.

00:02:56.762 --> 00:02:58.093
Quite a huge tanker.

00:02:58.093 --> 00:03:01.990
What is it?
The Aristimo I believe it's called.

00:03:06.538 --> 00:03:09.887
So legend has it in 1960,

00:03:09.887 --> 00:03:15.477
a big cyclone took place
in the Arabian Sea.

00:03:15.506 --> 00:03:19.452
and washed up a large wooden boat here

00:03:19.452 --> 00:03:24.446
and the locals dismantled it, salvaged it,

00:03:24.446 --> 00:03:30.169
sold the parts,
and then the opportunity was seen.

00:03:30.772 --> 00:03:34.825
The locals saw they could
salvage boats here,

00:03:34.825 --> 00:03:38.534
sell the raw materials in Karachi,
make a living.

00:03:39.435 --> 00:03:45.424
And so this whole beach
is about 10 kilometers.

00:03:46.675 --> 00:03:53.330
Roughly 135 different plots of beach

00:03:53.330 --> 00:03:55.302
for salvaging boats.

00:03:57.509 --> 00:04:01.157
Don't know if there's
any snakes here or not, Balochistan.

00:04:06.090 --> 00:04:08.423
Getting here was quite interesting.

00:04:09.177 --> 00:04:13.738
My driver said some of
the neighborhoods on the edge of Karachi

00:04:13.738 --> 00:04:16.826
were very dangerous

00:04:16.826 --> 00:04:20.679
and then when we got into
Balochistan it was a different feel.

00:04:20.679 --> 00:04:23.791
Huge Ranger presence.

00:04:24.421 --> 00:04:27.958
If you're not familiar with the Rangers

00:04:27.958 --> 00:04:30.425
they're sort of like military police.

00:04:30.658 --> 00:04:32.188
I don't think it's the army.

00:04:32.188 --> 00:04:35.178
It's like a separate branch.

00:04:35.178 --> 00:04:40.933
Okay, getting closer to the Aristimo.

00:04:43.017 --> 00:04:45.017
Can see the scraps over there.

00:04:46.717 --> 00:04:50.095
Think you can see it
in the GoPro in the distance.

00:04:50.095 --> 00:04:51.775
Lot of scrap metal here.

00:04:53.338 --> 00:04:55.788
It's crazy to think, what was it?

00:04:55.788 --> 00:05:00.057
1 million tons of metal
come out of this place.

00:05:02.744 --> 00:05:07.602
And so let's get into it,
let's investigate what the story is here.

00:05:08.563 --> 00:05:12.120
Oh, wall with glass and a ravine.

00:05:12.808 --> 00:05:13.808
Kay.

00:05:13.963 --> 00:05:16.430
Might be a bit more of a challenge...

00:05:18.232 --> 00:05:20.032
...than originally thought.

00:05:20.718 --> 00:05:23.051
There's a wall with glass up there.

00:05:23.986 --> 00:05:26.787
And a bit of a...

00:05:26.787 --> 00:05:29.299
Ah, sh*t, thorn up my shoe.

00:05:30.112 --> 00:05:31.152
Look at that.

00:05:31.897 --> 00:05:33.561
[grunts]

00:05:34.276 --> 00:05:35.487
God damnit

00:05:36.699 --> 00:05:37.735
[sighs]

00:05:37.735 --> 00:05:43.408
It's like a knife... [chuckles]
in the bottom of my foot.

00:05:44.253 --> 00:05:47.153
Okay, there are
a few barriers to entry here.

00:05:48.977 --> 00:05:55.071
Mega thorns, dried out moat, 
broken glass on the wall.

00:05:55.749 --> 00:06:02.448
So tread carefully and resume the mission.

00:06:04.122 --> 00:06:08.334
Okay, guys, we're on
more of an adventure than I first thought.-

00:06:08.977 --> 00:06:11.839
For some reason I thought it would be easy

00:06:11.839 --> 00:06:17.759
to just sort of get up onto the beach
and see them doing the work

00:06:17.759 --> 00:06:20.174
but it's not.

00:06:21.021 --> 00:06:23.344
Which is cool,
it makes it more interesting.

00:06:23.344 --> 00:06:25.024
Okay, this is like a...

00:06:26.878 --> 00:06:30.014
Seems like a road
for the workers to walk to work.

00:06:31.479 --> 00:06:36.133
It's not that fresh seaside smell
you might imagine.

00:06:37.013 --> 00:06:38.293
Smells like oil.

00:06:41.009 --> 00:06:47.116
I'm sure ecologically this isn't the best
thing that can happen for these beaches.

00:06:47.845 --> 00:06:50.198
Wow, look at that massive tanker.

00:06:50.198 --> 00:06:51.878
Looks like the front...

00:06:53.278 --> 00:06:56.130
The front was taken apart

00:06:56.130 --> 00:06:58.388
and they got a lot of work left.

00:06:58.388 --> 00:07:01.055
Look at all this machinery on the beach.

00:07:01.408 --> 00:07:02.408
Wow.

00:07:03.457 --> 00:07:06.323
And the sea, the sea looks quite beautiful.

00:07:07.162 --> 00:07:10.567
It actually looks blue, turquoise.

00:07:11.843 --> 00:07:17.258
Here, we have another boat
waiting to get pulled apart.

00:07:17.814 --> 00:07:19.393
[wind blowing]

00:07:20.587 --> 00:07:21.587
Wow.

00:07:22.305 --> 00:07:24.101
Moments like these, guys...

00:07:24.101 --> 00:07:26.780
This is what I love about travel.

00:07:26.780 --> 00:07:30.756
Just the discovery, and the randomness,

00:07:30.756 --> 00:07:36.074
and the surrealness
of situations like these.

00:07:36.934 --> 00:07:41.734
This beach is actually quite nice
and I'm surprised there's no litter on it.

00:07:42.020 --> 00:07:43.020
Wow.

00:07:44.208 --> 00:07:45.248
Look at this.

00:07:47.313 --> 00:07:48.593
[waves crashing]

00:07:49.350 --> 00:07:55.723
First goal is to get into
one of these ships and see the process.

00:07:56.508 --> 00:07:59.859
Second goal, find an English speaker.

00:07:59.859 --> 00:08:02.237
That might be a little challenging,

00:08:02.237 --> 00:08:05.628
and the third,
and probably most important goal

00:08:05.628 --> 00:08:07.659
is don't get kicked out.

00:08:09.753 --> 00:08:11.707
Like so many of the things...

00:08:11.707 --> 00:08:14.041
So many of the videos I do, it's...

00:08:15.204 --> 00:08:21.760
Do first and then
wait for the "No.", don't ask

00:08:21.760 --> 00:08:28.840
because when you ask for things like this
usually it draws a bizarre attention.

00:08:29.268 --> 00:08:31.335
There's a guy yelling up there.

00:08:31.762 --> 00:08:33.297
Look at this surreal scene.

00:08:33.297 --> 00:08:34.753
Oh my God.

00:08:35.253 --> 00:08:36.871
Absolutely stunning.

00:08:36.871 --> 00:08:38.483
These colors too.

00:08:39.748 --> 00:08:41.986
Guy's coming behind me.

00:08:42.602 --> 00:08:45.840
Just really want to get this shot
'cause how cool is that?

00:08:46.444 --> 00:08:47.444
Wow.

00:08:48.468 --> 00:08:51.627
It's like the mouth of a fish.

00:08:51.701 --> 00:08:53.320
[loud generator]

00:08:56.405 --> 00:08:57.690
Salam alaikum.

00:09:03.150 --> 00:09:04.720
[inaudible]

00:09:06.169 --> 00:09:07.849
Sir, can I get in there?

00:09:08.924 --> 00:09:09.924
In the ship?

00:09:11.187 --> 00:09:12.187
You and me?

00:09:16.044 --> 00:09:17.762
Can we go through the door?

00:09:17.762 --> 00:09:19.282
[man speaking inaudibly]

00:09:19.306 --> 00:09:20.306
No?

00:09:20.997 --> 00:09:22.365
I look, okay?

00:09:22.999 --> 00:09:24.679
[man speaking inaudibly]

00:09:28.841 --> 00:09:30.185
Wow.

00:09:36.276 --> 00:09:38.152
Salam alaikum.
-Wa alaik.

00:09:42.149 --> 00:09:45.202
Sir, can I go inside?

00:09:45.202 --> 00:09:46.347
[man speaking Arabic]

00:09:46.347 --> 00:09:47.707
Can we go inside?

00:09:49.079 --> 00:09:50.267
We go inside?

00:09:50.267 --> 00:09:51.947
[man speaking Arabic]

00:09:54.087 --> 00:09:56.887
Just gonna follow and get into this thing.

00:09:58.130 --> 00:09:59.130
[grunts]

00:09:59.503 --> 00:10:01.183
Okay, it's dark in here.

00:10:04.220 --> 00:10:07.011
This is what the inside
of an oil tanker looks like.

00:10:07.358 --> 00:10:08.621
Wow, before oil...

00:10:08.621 --> 00:10:10.301
[man speaking Arabic]

00:10:12.438 --> 00:10:13.668
Lot of echo.

00:10:18.652 --> 00:10:21.852
They're arguing over
if I should be in here or not.

00:10:23.347 --> 00:10:24.697
Acha. (Thank you)

00:10:24.878 --> 00:10:26.653
[loud boom]

00:10:26.653 --> 00:10:28.013
What's the noise?

00:10:28.013 --> 00:10:29.291
-Work, work, work.

00:10:29.291 --> 00:10:30.651
-Workers up there?

00:10:32.171 --> 00:10:33.858
[Arabic]

00:10:38.941 --> 00:10:41.061
Salam alaikum
-Wa alaikum salam.

00:10:41.618 --> 00:10:43.298
[men speaking Arabic]

00:10:45.419 --> 00:10:46.619
-Salam alaikum.

00:10:48.048 --> 00:10:50.828
Sir, we go in the door?

00:10:50.828 --> 00:10:52.508
[men speaking Arabic]

00:10:54.286 --> 00:10:55.286
Engine?

00:10:58.629 --> 00:11:00.762
Oh, they go up the ladder there.

00:11:02.660 --> 00:11:03.660
Okay.

00:11:04.167 --> 00:11:05.760
The goal is to get up to...

00:11:05.760 --> 00:11:07.059
Get up the ladder.

00:11:07.059 --> 00:11:09.059
Got one guy not allowing this.

00:11:13.654 --> 00:11:16.790
So all the workers were excited,
they wanted to...

00:11:17.148 --> 00:11:20.607
They were cool with taking me
up that ladder to get into the ship

00:11:20.607 --> 00:11:23.212
but there was one security guy there.

00:11:23.212 --> 00:11:24.572
Wasn't having it.

00:11:25.064 --> 00:11:32.313
So I managed to let them
let me ask the boss

00:11:32.313 --> 00:11:34.828
and the boss is up in this building,
the white building.

00:11:35.661 --> 00:11:38.357
And so that's where we're at.

00:11:39.053 --> 00:11:40.271
Asking the boss

00:11:40.271 --> 00:11:44.431
and I'm gonna put the camera down
because getting a lot of stares.

00:11:47.812 --> 00:11:49.979
Oh, I'm gonna keep it up.

00:11:50.728 --> 00:11:51.728
All right.

00:11:54.159 --> 00:11:55.458
Salam alaikum.

00:11:55.644 --> 00:11:57.576
[front end loader]

00:12:04.104 --> 00:12:05.555
Lot of friendly workers.

00:12:05.555 --> 00:12:07.553
Quite a surreal scene.

00:12:07.553 --> 00:12:10.511
Don't know if you're
feeling it on the camera

00:12:10.511 --> 00:12:12.846
but definitely a first.

00:12:13.645 --> 00:12:15.778
Salam alaikum.
-Wa alaikum salam.

00:12:18.805 --> 00:12:25.523
Can see all these parts just sectioned off,

00:12:25.523 --> 00:12:28.284
sold to the markets.

00:12:29.311 --> 00:12:31.569
I'm guessing all this goes to Karachi.

00:12:32.535 --> 00:12:33.646
Um...

00:12:36.578 --> 00:12:38.258
[man speaking Arabic]

00:13:24.649 --> 00:13:26.794
[hammering and machinery]

00:13:35.746 --> 00:13:37.143
[torch hissing]

00:13:40.707 --> 00:13:42.441
Those are massive engines.

00:13:49.203 --> 00:13:50.403
[diesel engine]

00:13:53.114 --> 00:13:54.404
[welding]

00:13:56.410 --> 00:13:58.090
[engines and machinery]

00:14:11.836 --> 00:14:13.116
[metal creaking]

00:14:21.711 --> 00:14:24.174
[man speaking off-camera]
Not allowed here.

00:14:24.174 --> 00:14:25.078
-What's that?

00:14:25.521 --> 00:14:28.054
All right, attempt number one, failed.

00:14:29.247 --> 00:14:32.228
There are 134 of these lots though.

00:14:32.228 --> 00:14:37.032
So the goal is to get onto another ship.

00:14:38.167 --> 00:14:41.067
Very nice people in there,
very accommodating.

00:14:42.719 --> 00:14:45.104
It's just the police shut it down.

00:14:45.382 --> 00:14:49.568
I think you can see behind me,
the homes where the workers live in.

00:14:49.568 --> 00:14:56.678
So they all work on the ships there
on the beach and then they live there too.

00:14:58.384 --> 00:15:02.099
So it seems like its own ecosystem.

00:15:02.813 --> 00:15:05.613
Unbelievable though, with all those parts.

00:15:06.600 --> 00:15:08.214
All that different machinery.

00:15:09.589 --> 00:15:13.049
There's so much that
goes into making a ship

00:15:13.049 --> 00:15:15.170
and taking it apart obviously.

00:15:16.225 --> 00:15:24.073
All right, back to the driver and then
try to figure out another plan here.

00:15:25.230 --> 00:15:32.150
I came out of the ship yard to my driver
and the police were there with him

00:15:32.150 --> 00:15:37.483
saying they gotta bring me
out of here ASAP, right now

00:15:37.483 --> 00:15:39.366
and nobody gets in trouble.

00:15:39.366 --> 00:15:42.102
So that was that, guys.

00:15:42.398 --> 00:15:49.818
That was a little flirtation with the ship
deconstruction in Balochistan, Pakistan.

00:15:50.694 --> 00:15:51.894
Until next one.

00:15:55.706 --> 00:15:59.092
And the third,
and probably the most important goal

00:15:59.092 --> 00:16:01.168
is don't get kicked out.

00:16:03.389 --> 00:16:04.669
[waves crashing]

